Better Skill Creator License
Version 1.0, 10 November 2026
Copyright RollingCodes

This license is the terms on which RollingCodes offers Better Skill Creator.
It is written so a reader can apply it without guessing. It is not a promise
that a court in every country will use these exact words.

Copies of this project that you already received under the Apache License 2.0
stay under that license. This file does not rewrite those older copies.

1. What this license covers

"This project" means the Better Skill Creator repository, its release tags,
the skill archive (the `.skill` file), and the Claude Code plugin zip, as
RollingCodes publishes them. It includes the source, the docs, the skill
instructions, the agent prompts, the tests, and the packaged archives.

"RollingCodes' work" means the original writing and code in this project that
RollingCodes authored. It includes the additions, rewrites, and arrangement
that make this repository Better Skill Creator rather than a checkout of
upstream skill-creator.

"Upstream material" means passages and files that come from Anthropic's
skill-creator and are still licensed under the Apache License 2.0. A copy of
that license is `LICENSE-APACHE-2.0` at the repository root, and
`LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt` beside the skill's `LICENSE.txt`. Those upstream
terms still apply to that material. This license does not remove them. The
Apache license does not give you permission to sell RollingCodes' work.

2. What you may do

You may use this project yourself, including on a computer you use for your
job. You may study it, and you may keep a private copy and a private
modification for that use.

You may use it to create a skill, a document, or another product that is not
this project. You may sell that product. Writing a skill with this tool is
not selling this project.

You may quote a short passage, with credit and a link to the official
repository, in a review, a lesson, or a bug report.

You may publish and sell an inspired version, as specified in section 4.

3. What you may not do

You may not sell this project. Selling includes a price, a subscription, a
paid download, a paid license, or any other payment for a copy, for access
to a copy, or for a hosted service whose product is this project. Bundling
this project into a paid course, a paid template pack, or a paid support
contract is selling it when the buyer is paying for this project.

You may not publicly reproduce this project. Public reproduction includes
posting the files, a release archive, or a packaged plugin for others to
download, mirroring the repository, or shipping those files inside another
download. Point people to the official repository instead.

You may not sublicense this project so someone else can do either of those
things.

These limits apply to the same thing, as specified in section 4. They apply
whether or not you changed the name, the colors, or a few files.

4. Specification: the same thing, and an inspired version

A work is the same thing as this project when any one of these is true:

1. It contains this repository, a release archive, or a packaged `.skill` or
   plugin zip, including after you rename files, wrap them in an installer,
   or compress them again.
2. It is offered under the names Better Skill Creator, skill-creator-local,
   or this project's branding, so a buyer would think they are getting this
   project.
3. It copies original source, skill instructions, agent prompts, schemas, or
   documentation from RollingCodes' work beyond a short quotation. A copy
   counts when a reader can match the wording, the command text, or the
   program structure to this project rather than to a new description of the
   same idea.
4. It is a mechanical transformation of this project: a translation, a
   reformatting, a minified or compiled form, or generated documentation of
   this source.
5. It is this project with a small change. Adding or removing a feature,
   changing a theme, or replacing the name, while the workflow, the command
   surface, and the original writing stay recognizably this project, leaves
   it the same thing.

A work is an inspired version, which you may publish and sell, only when all
of these are true:

1. You wrote it as a new work. You may reuse the ideas and the high-level
   goals, such as checking a skill, grading saved outputs, or packing a
   folder into an archive.
2. You did not copy this project's source, prompts, schemas, or docs, except
   for short quotations with credit.
3. You do not ship this repository, its release files, or its archives, and
   you do not tell buyers that they are buying Better Skill Creator.
4. A person comparing the two can see a different implementation: different
   code structure, different command text, and different written
   instructions. A renamed folder or a translated file is not a different
   implementation.

If you are unsure, treat the work as the same thing and do not sell it or
post it.

5. Credit

When you publish an inspired version, or when you quote this project, name
RollingCodes and link to
https://github.com/rolling-codes/better-skill-creator

6. No trademark grant

This license does not let you use the Better Skill Creator name or branding
for your product.

7. End of permission

If you sell or publicly reproduce the same thing, the permissions in this
license end for you. Sections 3 and 4 still describe what you must not do.

8. No warranty

This project is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind.
